  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Identity is a claim, not a URL",
      "items": [
        "the tenant comes from the validated token or the job payload — never from a query string and never from an unverified header",
        "@RolesAllowed and the container realm shape the UX; they are not tenant isolation. The use case decides identity, tenant, permission and ownership",
        "the database is the second line: tenant_id NOT NULL plus row-level security with a non-bypass application role"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "The template gap to close",
      "items": [
        "the worked example's WidgetResource still derives the tenant from security.getUserPrincipal().getName() with a \"public\" fallback, and says so in a comment",
        "replace it with the validated JWT tenant claim in your product — j2ee-review treats an unverified tenant as a Must-fix finding, not a note",
        "the same shape applies to a job: the payload carries tenantId and correlationId, and the consumer reads the tenant from there"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "The failure shape",
      "items": [
        "one ExceptionMapper per family: an invalid token answers 401, AppError.forbidden answers 403 with requiredPermission, a missing row answers 404",
        "a version mismatch is a typed conflict (409), never a 500; OptimisticLockException maps to conflict, and the exception never crosses the API",
        "the envelope is { \"error\": { code, message, requiredPermission, correlationId } } — a stack trace, SQL text or an internal id never leaves the server"
      ]
    }
  ]
